Final Round – Client Interview Experience (DevOps Engineer) 🚀

In my final client round, the panel included 2 AWS Cloud Architects and 1 Project Manager. The Project Manager began by explaining the project, which is a large-scale migration project to AWS. After that, the Cloud Architects asked me technical questions to assess my skills and real-world problem-solving ability.

Questions I was asked in this round:

1️⃣ How have you used Terraform to structure and modularize infrastructure for different environments?

2️⃣ How do you typically manage Terraform state files, and why use remote storage with S3 and DynamoDB?

3️⃣ What has been your experience in building CI/CD pipelines to make deployments smoother and more reliable?

4️⃣ Can you explain your exposure to EKS and how you manage application traffic inside the cluster?

5️⃣ How would you troubleshoot a case where an EC2 instance has an IAM role for S3 access but still gets “Permission Denied”?

6️⃣ What is AWS API Gateway, and what is it mainly used for?

7️⃣ How do you handle application rollbacks in Kubernetes with Argo CD?

8️⃣ What approach would you take for blue-green deployments as compared to rolling updates?

9️⃣ During Kubernetes upgrades with limited nodes, how do you minimize downtime and ensure stability?

🔟 In a migration project, what steps would you take to ensure security, cost optimization, and smooth transition to AWS?

This final round was a mix of project-level discussion and deep technical questions around Terraform, EKS, CI/CD, and AWS services. It gave me a great opportunity to showcase both my technical expertise and my ability to work on a critical migration project.
